---
import traditionalTextSeriesIcon from '../../../assets/icons/traditional_text_series.svg?url';
import contemporaryClinicalSeriesIcon from '../../../assets/icons/contemporary_clinical_series.svg?url';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout heroClass="online-courses-hero">
    <div slot="hero" class="online-courses-banner">
        <h1>Online Courses</h1>
    </div>

    <section class="courses-discovery">
        <div class="courses-list">
            <a href="/course-detail.html" class="course-card-link">
                <article class="course-card">
                    <div class="course-card-main">
                        <div class="course-tag">Traditional Text Series</div>
                        <h3>Dr. Wang’s Lectures on <i></i>Jin Gui Yao Lue (Essential from the Golden Cabinet)</h3>
                        <p class="course-instructor">Dr. Sanhu Wang</p>
                        <p class="course-description">A systematic study of the <i>Jin Gui Yao Lue (Essential from the Golden Cabinet)</i> with emphasis on modern clinical importance. Often considered to proceed <i>Shang Han Lun (Treatise on Cold Injury)</i>, Zhang Zhong Jing’s Jin Gui Yao Lue provides methodologies in the study, diagnosis, and treatment of a variety of diseases. The text is as precise, profound as Shang Han Lun, and its topics arguably much more relevant. Our offering is the first systematic teaching of the <i>>Jin Gui Yao Lue</i> in English. <br><br>
                        
                        Dr. Sanhu Wang is a medical doctor, chief physician, and professor of medicine at Xi’An TCM hospital, with over four decades of clinical experience. Named as a Renowned TCM Practitioner in both Shaanxi and Guangxi provinces, Dr. Wang is a leading figure in the field for in applying classical texts and formulas in treating modern diseases. Dr. Wang’s lecture series on the Jin Gui Yao Lue was selected among a survey of more than ten difference sources in Chinese, for its accuracy, depth, and the balance between orthodoxy and progressiveness. <br><br>

                        It is recommend to study the series as a whole in sequence, but the teachings, categorized by disease type, can also accommodate plug-in-and-use style learning. Familiarity of the Shang Han Lun is helpful but not required for understanding of this text.</p>
                    </div>
                </article>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="tracks">
        <h2>Two Tracks, One Medicine</h2>
        <div class="tracks-row">
            <div class="track">
                <img src={traditionalTextSeriesIcon} alt="Traditional Text Series icon">
                <h3>Traditional Text Series</h3>
                <p>Deepen your conceptual and theoretical understanding of the medicine with foundational texts taught by TCM masters. For practitioners who want to return to the source.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="track track--with-divider">
                <img src={contemporaryClinicalSeriesIcon} alt="Contemporary Clinical Series icon">
                <h3>Contemporary Clinical Series</h3>
                <p>Learn directly from the clinic room. Take in diagnostic thinkings, case strategies, and clinical insights from experts steeped in the robust clinical scene at top TCM hospitals in China.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <Fragment slot="scripts">
        <script>
            import '../../../scripts/main.js';
        </script>
    </Fragment>
</BaseLayout>
